  "governing_obligation": "Every RFC/WFM workbook first produces exact-source staging before mutation; valid source presence remains distinct from proposal acceptance so rejected/deferred/unresolved changes cannot fabricate disappearance. Safe target dispositions occur at the smallest explainable idempotent scope; auto-accept is limited to approved low-risk classes and excludes terminal, hierarchy, ownership, timeframe, disappearance, empty-population, and competing-attempt cases; disputed terminal RFCs remain individually reviewable, accepted terminal evidence plus pending cascade proposal commit atomically while cascade execution remains separately protected, and whole-import rejection is reserved for genuine workbook-level integrity/identity/chronology/scope/safety/inseparable-consistency failure.",
